Expected elements: present

Register fidelity is genuinely good — dark, dense, mono-textured, with the desktop app's file tab strip, loop-iteration chips, inline value pills, depth guides and a phase rail that names and quantifies. Nothing here reads as the explorer inverted.

The five changes: (1) landed, and is the round's win — the provenance paragraph (y232–355) now spans the pane flush-left in six lines instead of eleven, and FEE PAYER / TARGET recovered their column. It is not too quiet: the badge is the pane's only blue-outlined chip. (2) not verifiable — the only cost row in view is `COST · MANA` (y633), base ten; the fee row sits below the pane's unsignalled clip at y1080. (3) only the no-calldata sentence renders here; it is state-specific and well-formed. (4) landed at line 29 (`⊘`) and line 32 (`⊙`), but inconsistently. (5) landed in the exit (`← demo`, x22–77); prose residue remains.

The queued observation stands. `Status reason: private-part-succeeded-public-part-succeeded` (y155–186) is still a raw kebab enum, and because it sits ABOVE the DATA row it is the first prose a reader meets in the pane carrying this register's honesty claim. `sentenceCase` exists in `client/src/viewutil.nim` and is not applied; capitalisation alone would not fix it. The `Partial` badge and the EXECUTIONS group already say this, so deleting the line is defensible.

Highest-priority fixes: humanise or drop the status reason; extend `⊘` to every unrun arm.

Rating: 7/10

